THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL

The benchmark values in refsol/benchmarks.py are numerical results published in:

    G. R. Hadley, "High-accuracy finite-difference equations for dielectric
    waveguide analysis II: dielectric corners", J. Lightwave Technol. 20(7),
    1210-1218 (2002). doi:10.1109/JLT.2002.800370

They were cross-checked against the same values as tabulated in the benchmark
documentation of the femwell project (GPL-3.0,
https://github.com/HelgeGehring/femwell). Only the measured/computed values
themselves are reproduced here -- no code, text, or other expressive content
from femwell is included in or derived from this package, and this package is
not a derivative work of femwell.

The NAFEMS T4 problem statement and its target temperature (18.3 degC at
(0.6, 0.2) m) in refsol/thermal_convection.py are published benchmark facts,
reproduced as quoted by two public documents that cite NAFEMS:

    DIANA FEA, "Two-Dimensional Heat Transfer with Convection",
    https://tutorials.dianafea.com/2DHeatTransferConvection.pdf
    (citing NAFEMS, "The Standard NAFEMS Benchmarks", 1990)

    FEATool Multiphysics, ex_heattransfer4.m,
    https://www.featool.com/doc/ex__heattransfer4_8m
    (citing A. D. Cameron, J. A. Casey, G. B. Simpson, "Benchmark Tests for
    Thermal Analysis", NAFEMS, 1986)

Only the numbers are reproduced; no text, code or figures from NAFEMS, DIANA
FEA or FEATool are included in or derived from this package.
